! jb_ax3a "IBOX-3", routine 1222 section I2221, pp.139-140 (octal
! 030167.00-030214.40): "CHECK SVA TO 3 MEMS, DATA BIT 22" and "...
! DATA BIT 23" -- SVA into a FULL-WORD instruction, the 24-bit width.
!
! WHY THIS BLOCK.  ibox3_sva_fp pins SVA's 18-bit width and
! ibox3_sva_dix pins the 19-bit width.  The third width, 24, was
! implemented from Ref. Manual p.29 alone and had NO test: both of the
! other blocks' templates are half-length (I22K2 op 0x60, I22K4 op
! 0x30), so the `instrLen(h) == Full` arm of dirIndexOp's SVA was
! unreachable by the whole suite.  MEASURED, not assumed: with that arm
! forced to the 19-bit path, all 274 sections that existed before this
! one still pass.  The gap was real, and this section is what closes
! it -- under the same injection this block halts at SERS with SEN =
! 030176.00, its FIRST check, "SVA above bit to ext mem failed".
!
! AND THE LISTING STATES THE RULE, which the Reference Manual does not.
! p.140, in the comment block that closes this series:
!
!   1. IF BIT 27 IS 1, INSTRUCTION IS DIRECT INDEX, STORE 19 BITS.
!   2. IF BITS 26 AND 27 ARE 10, INSTRUCTIO IS FP, STORE 18 BITS.
!   3. IF BITS 25-27 ARE 100, INSTRUCT IS CB OR BIND, STORE 19 BITS.
!   4. IF BITS 24-27 ARE 1000, INSTRUCT IS FULL WD, STORE 24 BITS.
!   5. IF BITS 23-27 ARE 10000, INSTRUCT IS IMMED IX, STORE 19 BITS.
!   6. IF BITS 23-27 ARE 00000, INSTRUCT IS MISC, STORE 19 BITS.
!
! That is the machine's own length tag, read outward from bit 27: the
! six patterns partition bits 23-27 exactly (xxxx1, xxx10, xx100,
! x1000, 10000, 00000), so the ladder is a decision, not a priority
! order.  And it agrees case for case with what the model does by
! running decodeHalfWord -- FP -> 18, the full-word tag -> 24,
! everything else (cases 1, 3, 5, 6) -> 19.  It is worth having in the
! repository in the deck's own words, because p.29 gives only the three
! numbers and one misleading note about TRANSMIT/SWAP.
!
! (Case 2's "INSTRUCTIO" is the listing's typo, kept as printed.)
!
! HOW IT PROVES 24 RATHER THAN 19.  The template I22K1 is "$L%BU,0", a
! full-word VFL Load whose address field is zero; the test values are
! IBIT22 and IBIT23, single bits at value positions 22 and 23 -- ABOVE
! a 19-bit field (0-18).  Store, read back, compare for EQUALITY:
!
!   24 bits stored  ->  the bit lands, KV compares equal, BXE taken
!   19 bits stored  ->  bits 19-23 keep the template's zeros, the
!                       value reads back 0, KV is unequal, and the
!                       block halts on "SVA ABOVE BIT TO ... FAILED"
!
! The IBITs are NEGATIVE ("%8-0.02"): their sign bit is 1, and so is
! the template's, so the comparison is of two like-signed values and
! the equality turns on the magnitude field alone.
!
! AND IT DOES ALL THREE MEMORIES per bit, which neither earlier block
! does: I22WRK (external), $R (word 9, internal memory) and $X1 itself
! (word 17, index core storage).  The three NOPs between the last
! store and the first read-back are the listing's own settling gap.
!
! -- SSIP framework substitutes: SERS (octal 1304) -> FAIL halt,
! -- SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch for SIC.
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants for 1222 (p.165) --
        SLC, (8)31301.0
IBIT22  XW, -(8)0.02, 0, 0                   ! test wd: bit 22, negative
IBIT23  XW, -(8)0.01, 0, 0                   ! test wd: bit 23, negative
! I22K1 is "$L%BU,0": a VFL Load with the default data description.
! Its bits 24-27 are 1000 -- the full-word length tag, case 4 above.
I22K1   L, 0.0
! I22WRK is "DR%BU,64,8,%1%" in the listing -- a RESERVED word, a
! pseudo-op this assembler does not have.  A zeroed word is the same
! thing here: the block stores the template into it before every use.
        SLC, (8)31322.0
I22WRK  DD(BU,64,8), 0

        SLC, (8)30167.0
I2221   LX, $X0, IBIT22                      ! check SVA to 3 mems, data bit 22.
        LX, $X1, I22K1
        SX, $X1, I22WRK
        SVA, $X0, I22WRK
        SX, $X1, $R
        SVA, $X0, $R
        SVA, $X0, $X1
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        KV, $X0, I22WRK
        BXE, $+1.32
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS                              ! SVA above bit to ext mem failed.
        KV, $X0, $R
        BXE, $+1.32
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS                              ! SVA above bit to int mem failed.
        KV, $X0, $X1
        BXE, $+1.32
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS                              ! SVA above bit to ix core stg failed.

        LX, $X0, IBIT23                      ! check SVA to 3 mems, data bit 23.
        LX, $X1, I22K1
        SX, $X1, I22WRK
        SVA, $X0, I22WRK
        SX, $X1, $R
        SVA, $X0, $R
        SVA, $X0, $X1
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        KV, $X0, I22WRK
        BXE, $+1.32
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS                              ! SVA above bit to ext mem failed.
        KV, $X0, $R
        BXE, $+1.32
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS                              ! SVA above bit to int mem failed.
        KV, $X0, $X1
        BXE, $+1.32
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS                              ! SVA above bit to ix core stg failed.
I2221A  BEW, $
        END, I2221
